    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Two-week review of sleep, nightmares and drinking, seen the same day by psychiatry. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Geronimo returns two weeks after intake, with the interpreter, and is seen the same day by Dr. Achebe-Varga, the visiting psychiatrist, who completed the CAPS-5 interview with him this morning. He still sleeps three or four hours a night, with nightmares most nights, and wakes ready to fight. He has cut his drinking from five or six drinks to three or four most evenings, and takes thiamine. His intake tests showed a PEth of 236 ng/mL, AST 58 and GGT 112 U/L with normal kidney function, albumin and bilirubin. A urine test today shows no opioids. He has not fallen again. He would like to try the talking treatment first and is not ready for a medicine for his mood; he will take a medicine for the drinking. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Three or four hours; nightmares most nights</td></tr><tr><td>Drinking</td><td>Three or four drinks most evenings, down from five or six</td></tr><tr><td>PCL-5</td><td>54</td></tr><tr><td>CAPS-5</td><td>Criteria met in all four symptom clusters; severity 44</td></tr><tr><td>Urine drug test</td><td>No opioids</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Positive</td><td>Nightmares, unwanted memories, startle and poor sleep; no thoughts of suicide</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Negative</td><td>No tremor, sweats or confusion when he drinks less</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No abdominal pain, jaundice or black stools</td></tr><tr><td>Musculoskeletal</td><td>Negative</td><td>Left hip bruise healing; no pain on walking</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

